{% include "kb/_abstraction_rules.j2" %}
Task: produce ONE revised markdown playbook document, and nothing else (no
preamble, no commentary, no code fences around the whole thing). The document
MUST match the shape of the existing playbook. A deterministic Python
validator will reject your output if any of these constraints are violated:

- Every `##` section (Summary, Symptoms, Triage Procedure, Verification
  Procedure, Required Evidence (Submission Gate), Known Distractors, Failure
  Patterns) must be present, in order, with the exact heading text.
- The `<!-- meta -->` block must contain the keys `slug`, `class_name`,
  `seen`, `created_from`, `last_updated`, each on its own line as `key: value`.
- Symptoms, Triage Procedure, Verification Procedure, and Required Evidence
  must each be non-empty.
- Required Evidence must contain at least one `- [ ]` checkbox item, and
  every item there must be a `- [ ]` checkbox.
- The following vague phrases are FORBIDDEN anywhere in the document:
  "appropriate values", "as needed", "relevant configuration", "if applicable",
  "as appropriate". Use parameterized placeholders (`<ENV_VAR>`,
  `<NAMESPACE>`, `<DEPLOYMENT>`, ...) for incident-specific tokens — those
  are precise, not vague — and write concrete commands and shapes around
  them.

Refinement rules (you are FREE to rewrite, not just append):
- You MAY rewrite any section — Summary, Symptoms, Triage, Verification,
  Required Evidence, Distractors — wherever the existing wording would have
  let this failure through. Free rewrite is encouraged where it improves
  precision.
- If the existing playbook contains any incident-specific tokens (literal
  namespaces, deployment names, env var names, error strings, port numbers,
  pod hashes, references to specific incidents) baked into ANY section, you
  MUST rewrite those sections to use parameterized placeholders per the
  abstraction rules above. The existing playbook's specifics are evidence,
  not prescription — strip them out of the document entirely. If the
  existing playbook contained a `## References` section, drop it; the
  current schema does not include one.
- You MUST preserve all existing Failure Patterns and Known Distractors that
  remain accurate (rewriting them in the abstract, parameterized form if
  they were too incident-specific). ADD a new Failure Pattern entry for each
  item in `recovery_stage_failures`, of the shape:
    - **<stage>:** "<abstracted description, parameterized>". **Oracle:** <abstracted correction>. **Lesson:** <general lesson>.
- New Triage / Verification / Required Evidence content must be grounded in
  `recovery_observations` and the oracle answer — do not invent steps
  recovery did not perform — but written as the abstract pattern those
  observations reveal, with concrete tokens parameterized.
- The class_name and slug must remain unchanged from the existing playbook.
- In the `<!-- meta -->` block:
    - `slug:` stays as {{ slug }}
    - `class_name:` stays as {{ class_name }}
    - `seen:` MUST be incremented by 1 from the existing playbook's value
    - `created_from:` keep whatever the existing playbook had
    - `last_updated:` MUST be updated to {{ current_iso }}

If the existing playbook is malformed or missing a section, repair it as
part of this revision — the validator will check the output, not the input.

Output the revised markdown document only. Begin with
`# Playbook: {{ class_name }}`.
